\begin_layout Subsection*
Why the Analytical Hierarchy Process (AHP)?
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
AHP provides an axiomatic framework (
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "Saaty1986"
literal "false"

\end_inset

) for 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

...logic and reasoning with the aid of very small samples of data
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 (
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "Ehrig2026"
literal "false"

\end_inset

).
 It is a multi-criterion decision methodology (MCDM) enjoying widespread applicability to group decision making (
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "Saaty1994"
literal "false"

\end_inset

),
 risk analysis (e.g.,
 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "Saaty1987,Vaidya2006,Linkov2006"
literal "false"

\end_inset

),
 and other problems.
 AHP is often applied to situations where substantial amounts of statistically coherent measurements are not immediately available to support more-empirical approaches.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The AHP methodology begins with identifying a plausible 
\emph on
evidentiary span
\emph default
:
 The range of measurable factors —
 
\emph on
elements
\emph default
 in the vernacular of 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "Saaty1986,Saaty1994"
literal "false"

\end_inset

 —
 believed to differentiate within the range of scenarios under consideration.
 A 
\emph on
hierarchy model
\emph default
 represents such spans as tree graphs.
 The responsible individual decision maker or a panel of experts then performs
\emph on
 comparative judgements
\emph default
:
 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

...the numerical representation of a relationship between two elements that share a common parent
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 in the tree graph (
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "Saaty1994"
literal "false"

\end_inset

).
 A case study herein demonstrates AHP's use to rank plausible alternatives.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Not strictly a stand-alone method,
 AHP can be fused with other approaches.
 Bayesian techniques allow for subsequent revision of the comparative judgements as stronger empirical evidence emerges (
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "Merrick2005,LiH2025"
literal "false"

\end_inset

).
 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "LiJ2025"
literal "false"

\end_inset

