 it is about the structure of reasoning...
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 (quoted in 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "Pearl1988"
literal "false"

\end_inset

,
 p.
 15).
 The AHP methodology contains mechanisms to identify inconsistencies and contradictions in the structure of reasoning (
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "Saaty2003,Pant2022"
literal "false"

\end_inset

).
 Here,
 we consider the types of inconsistencies in comparative judgements from which concerns might arise.
 We then review 
\emph on
consistency indices
\emph default
,
 AHP's mechanism to quantify the degree of inconsistency.
 Finally,
 we consider alternative graph-theoretic approaches to mitigate inconsistencies in reasoning.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "Saaty1986"
literal "false"

\end_inset

 contains an extensive set of definitions,
 axioms,
 and theorems culminating in the demonstration that,
 if the eigenvector/eigenvalue decomposition of a 
\emph on
perfectly consistent
\emph default
 reciprocal matrix 
\begin_inset Formula $\boldsymbol{A}_{\mathfrak{H}}$
\end_inset

 is
\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

\backslash
begin{subequations}
\end_layout

\end_inset


\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{equation}
\boldsymbol{A}_{\mathfrak{H}}\boldsymbol{X}_{\mathfrak{H}}=\boldsymbol{X}_{\mathfrak{H}}\boldsymbol{\Lambda}_{\mathfrak{H}}\mbox{,}\label{eq:general-reciprocal-eigendecomposition}
\end{equation}

\end_inset

then 
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{equation}
\lambda_{\mathfrak{H}}=n\label{eq:reciprocal-consistency-condition}
\end{equation}

\end_inset


\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

\backslash
end{subequations}
\end_layout

\end_inset

where 
\begin_inset Formula $n$
\end_inset

 denotes the order of 
\begin_inset Formula $\boldsymbol{A}_{\mathfrak{H}}$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $\lambda_{\mathfrak{H}}=[\boldsymbol{\Lambda}_{\mathfrak{H}}]_{\text{argmax}(\boldsymbol{\Lambda}_{\mathfrak{H}})}$
\end_inset

.
 Such a matrix invariantly satisfies (
